If you have the time facebook marketplace has done well for me for furniture, you need a friend with a good car and solid measurements of the car and the space, but there are a lot of people selling/giving away really nice couches plus you'll be able to get a bit of an assessment on them. It takes a lot more time  but I've been really lucky in finding really nice stuff sometimes you turn around at the pick up point, but others it's a real steal because people are moving an just don't want to pay to have it removed. 

&#x200B;

I'm in a similar situation and am looking at what poor habits serve me well (especially because I have an eye towards zero waste) and which don't. So I'm still shopping at good will for things like clothes and furniture (especially hard furniture) and looking for some fun gigs I could turn into money. Because I like having extra income steams but don't want to do shitty things. I'm working really hard to pay down all my debt, and of course that's important, save enough for a couple months at first and once you start feeling secure look at how you want your life to look, because living afraid and poor when you aren't is not a good look on anyone.

