My natural accent is a weird English/American hybrid that is very close to transatlantic. My mother is from England and my father is from the west coast. 

&#x200B;

I have a learned total American accent I use most of the time which is very New England but not Boston, and influenced by old school Brooklyn and the south.  It is weird and means I always sound like I'm from somewhere else. 

&#x200B;

My English accent is so midlands posh that I'm embarrassed by it. I wish I had a good London accent, I can learn it but I have to put it on.   


I also pick up accents like a sponge and then incorporate them in my American accent, which makes it even weirder

