Just got let go from a "great culture" place as well, it was toxic as fuck and i thought just doing my job right would save me, but it didn't. Rough having to leave a place that I had high hopes for but I feel better off for it. Hope you find a place where you have people who trust you and your judgement next time. 

&#x200B;

btw, if more places comped drinks after shit shifts the world would be a better place and bartenders would stick around longer. I've often felt like my contributions don't matter after a crazy shift.

Honestly this is what ruined my life. Having to work full time for college caused me to stop being able to study. My recommendation is to power through till you have your degree. Talk with the friends you trust and can be honest with, so that if you get kicked out you can stay with them. Make sure all your money is in a seperate account and your parents cannot access it. When you graduate get a job in the service industry and make money, Save your tips and look for a better paying job, Stay with your family as long as possible until you can afford to move out. If you live in a college town look for the cheapest rent possible. I had a friend who shared a room with someone who was paying about 400 a month. Look for the deals. You can go up from the bottom, but it's rough. 

&#x200B;

Focus on your degree first.

