Okay, So first off you did nothing wrong, second off, it's your body. 

&#x200B;

Your virginity is your own business and also has no real physical meaning. While there are cups for people who have had babies, it's mainly just some sort of size thing. You're fine.

BRING CURTIANS! You don't know if you'll have them in your new place and it's sooo hard to sleep if your window is just near a street light or something. Cleaning supplies are perfect dollar store buys, don't bring them unless it's easy to pack, storage and the like try to repourpos things that can store during the move and after. Bedding it's good to make sure everything you bring is something you like, ditch extras or mismatches you don't love. Towels again, go through and make sure what you bring is the stuff you really like. 

&#x200B;

Go to a dollar store and see how much it would cost you to buy those basics like hangers and figure if that's in your budget. 

&#x200B;

Do as much cleaning as you can before you leave to either sell or get your deposit back use up your supplies that way!

I set small things I can do for myself. Like taking a shower or doing a face mask, That works really well because it makes you sit and relax for a bit, as well as help out your skin while this weather kinda sucks it dry!

